From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:37:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: build SQLite's recovery into application-services'
 SQLite

sql-support compiles SQLite's recovery extension, sqlite3recover.c and
dbdata.c from SQLite 3.50.2's ext/recover/, copied unchanged from the
check-in of the amalgamation libsqlite3-sys bundles, against that
amalgamation, which is now built with SQLITE_ENABLE_DBPAGE_VTAB: the
recovery reads a database page by page through sqlite_dbpage. For
obfsvfs's repair of a damaged sealed database.

Cargo takes a vendored crate as it was last built, by its version
alone, so an objdir built before this needs libsqlite3-sys's build
removed for the flag to take.

The stage 3 spike's patch 0010 (encriox W25).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
